      "writtenOn": "2022-01-29T00:44:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should the most common case (\"Success\") have its own variant? Something like:\n\n  #define binder_reset_extended_error(thread) \\\n          do { \\\n              thread-\u003eextended_error.ee_code \u003d BINDER_EE_CODE_OK; \\\n\t      thread-\u003eextended_error.ee_type \u003d BINDER_EE_TYPE_NONE; \\\n\t      thread-\u003eextended_error.ee_string[0] \u003d \u0027\\0\u0027; \\\n\t  } while (0)\n\n(avoids the needless strnprint in the success case)",
      "revId": "8231081adb3515bb77d87c7475a7e17dfb9d6ac6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
