      },
      "lineNbr": 287,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T21:42:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "there currently is a `binder_user_debug()` that could leverage the new populated `ee-\u003estrings` as this:\n```\nbinder_set_extended_error(ee, ..., \"no transaction stack\");\nbinder_user_error(\"%d:%d %s\\n\", proc-\u003epid, thread-\u003epid, ee-\u003estring);\n```\nBecause as I was writing these `ee-\u003estrings` I noticed duplication with `binder_user_error()` in most cases. So do we want to go down this path?\n\nThe downside is we don\u0027t want to extend this `ee-\u003estring` buffer too large as you mention in previous comments.",
      "parentUuid": "a3ddcf49_80526d4d",
      "revId": "8231081adb3515bb77d87c7475a7e17dfb9d6ac6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
